00:25:39.158 --> 00:25:41.140
- You're the best. (indistinct)

00:25:41.140 --> 00:25:42.750
(flames crackling)

00:25:42.750 --> 00:25:45.450
- [Kimia] And now, a word-for-word scene

00:25:45.450 --> 00:25:47.880
from season two, episode 22,

00:25:47.880 --> 00:25:51.559
of Angela's favorite show,
Aaron Sorkin's "The West Wing."

00:25:51.559 --> 00:25:52.530
(Angela squealing)

00:25:52.530 --> 00:25:54.543
We take you to a church.

00:25:55.400 --> 00:25:56.402
(Angela clapping)

00:25:56.402 --> 00:25:59.152
(crew laughing)

00:26:01.920 --> 00:26:03.270
- She bought her first new car

00:26:03.270 --> 00:26:04.880
and you hit her with a drunk driver.

00:26:04.880 --> 00:26:05.971
(crew spitting water simultaneously)

00:26:05.971 --> 00:26:07.470
(everyone laughing)

00:26:07.470 --> 00:26:09.262
Oh, was that supposed to be funny?

00:26:09.262 --> 00:26:10.095
(Angela laughing)

00:26:10.095 --> 00:26:10.928
(everyone laughing)
(bell chiming)

00:26:10.928 --> 00:26:12.570
"You can't conceive, nor can I,

00:26:12.570 --> 00:26:16.950
the strangeness of the mercy
of God," said Graham Greene.

00:26:16.950 --> 00:26:19.080
I don't know whose ass
he was kissin' there,

00:26:19.080 --> 00:26:20.580
but I think you're just vindictive.

00:26:20.580 --> 00:26:21.720
Say it with me.

00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:23.070
What was Josh Lyman?

00:26:23.070 --> 00:26:24.393
A warning shot?

00:26:25.688 --> 00:26:27.008
He was my son!

00:26:27.008 --> 00:26:28.459
(crew laughing)

00:26:28.459 --> 00:26:29.292
What did I ever do

00:26:29.292 --> 00:26:31.710
except praise your glory
and praise his name?

00:26:31.710 --> 00:26:34.792
There's a tropical storm
that's gaining speed and power.

00:26:34.792 --> 00:26:36.780
(Angela and crew laughing)

00:26:36.780 --> 00:26:40.110
They say it's as strong as
the storm that you built

00:26:40.110 --> 00:26:43.014
that took out a tender ship
last year in the North Atlantic.

00:26:43.014 --> 00:26:44.070
(everyone laughing)

00:26:44.070 --> 00:26:45.030
68 crew.

00:26:45.030 --> 00:26:46.680
You know what a tender ship does?

00:26:46.680 --> 00:26:47.883
It fixes other ships.

00:26:49.020 --> 00:26:49.853
Yeah.

00:26:49.853 --> 00:26:50.686
That's all it does.

00:26:50.686 --> 00:26:51.540
Hold on.
(everyone laughing)

00:26:51.540 --> 00:26:52.980
It doesn't even carry guns.

00:26:52.980 --> 00:26:54.720
It floats around and fixes other ships

00:26:54.720 --> 00:26:55.890
and delivers that mail.

00:26:55.890 --> 00:26:57.331
That's all it can do.

00:26:57.331 --> 00:27:01.260
(stammering) Gratias tibi ago, domine.

00:27:01.260 --> 00:27:03.180
There's a lotta Latin in this.

00:27:03.180 --> 00:27:04.620
Yes, I lied!

00:27:04.620 --> 00:27:06.202
Yes, it was a sin!

00:27:06.202 --> 00:27:07.292
(everyone laughing)

00:27:07.292 --> 00:27:08.513
- (laughing) He's so wet.

00:27:10.050 --> 00:27:11.490
- I've committed many sins.

00:27:11.490 --> 00:27:15.030
Have I displeased you, you feckless dog?

00:27:15.030 --> 00:27:16.560
3.8 million new jobs.

00:27:16.560 --> 00:27:17.940
That wasn't good?

00:27:17.940 --> 00:27:20.250
Bailed out Mexico,
increased foreign trade,

00:27:20.250 --> 00:27:22.350
30 million new acres of conservation!

00:27:22.350 --> 00:27:23.760
Put Mendoza on the bench!

00:27:23.760 --> 00:27:25.110
We're not fighting a war!

00:27:25.110 --> 00:27:26.340
I've raised three children!

00:27:26.340 --> 00:27:28.539
That's not enough to buy
me outta the dog house?

00:27:28.539 --> 00:27:30.030
(everyone laughing)

00:27:30.030 --> 00:27:34.345
(Patrick speaking in Latin)

00:27:34.345 --> 00:27:38.845
(Patrick continues speaking in Latin)

00:27:43.765 --> 00:27:44.671
- Yeah!

00:27:44.671 --> 00:27:49.008
(everyone cheering and applauding)

00:27:49.008 --> 00:27:50.425
That was so good!

00:27:52.590 --> 00:27:54.240
You really did it!

00:27:54.240 --> 00:27:55.590
- I had it memorized.

00:27:55.590 --> 00:27:56.880
- No, that's too much work.

00:27:56.880 --> 00:27:58.500
- Five years ago, Angela had a birthday

00:27:58.500 --> 00:28:00.100
where she made everyone bring a monologue.

00:28:00.100 --> 00:28:01.550
- [Chanse] Oh, no.

00:28:01.550 --> 00:28:03.689
- It was karaoke, but monologue.

00:28:03.689 --> 00:28:05.001
- I love that.

00:28:05.001 --> 00:28:05.922
- And I did this exact monologue.

00:28:05.922 --> 00:28:07.410
- And he did this, and he did it so well,

00:28:07.410 --> 00:28:08.550
but ya did it even better today.

00:28:08.550 --> 00:28:09.383
- Thank you.

00:28:09.383 --> 00:28:10.911
- Wow.
- Yay!

00:28:10.911 --> 00:28:12.089
- You get Hoynes!

00:28:12.089 --> 00:28:13.382
- You get Hoynes!

00:28:13.382 --> 00:28:14.215
What was Josh Lyman?

00:28:14.215 --> 00:28:15.690
A warning shot?

00:28:15.690 --> 00:28:17.400
He's very metered and then he loses it.

00:28:17.400 --> 00:28:18.703
And that's God, isn't it?

00:28:18.703 --> 00:28:20.940
(flames crackling)

00:28:20.940 --> 00:28:21.873
- Hello, Angela.

00:28:23.610 --> 00:28:26.599
You kept screaming at me this
week to dial it back, so...

00:28:26.599 --> 00:28:27.870
(Angela spitting water)
(bell chiming)

00:28:27.870 --> 00:28:29.180
I haven't even done it yet.

00:28:29.180 --> 00:28:30.630
(everyone laughing)

00:28:30.630 --> 00:28:33.282
So I'm gonna pitch you something

00:28:33.282 --> 00:28:34.592
instead of doing the full thing.

00:28:34.592 --> 00:28:35.730
(Angela awing)

00:28:35.730 --> 00:28:37.274
This is "Angela: The Musical."

00:28:37.274 --> 00:28:38.410
(Eli gasping)

00:28:38.410 --> 00:28:40.369
(everyone laughing)

00:28:40.369 --> 00:28:42.482
(poster flapping)

00:28:42.482 --> 00:28:43.770
(bell chiming)

00:28:43.770 --> 00:28:45.540
Okay, it's not all memorized.

00:28:45.540 --> 00:28:46.890
And I'll be playing multiple parts.

00:28:46.890 --> 00:28:49.327
I'll be playing the part of
Angela and everyone else.

00:28:49.327 --> 00:28:50.880
(everyone laughing)

00:28:50.880 --> 00:28:52.149
You can cue it.

00:28:52.149 --> 00:28:53.790
(Courtney gasping)

00:28:53.790 --> 00:28:56.670
We go to the set of
"Thor 2: The Dark World,"

00:28:56.670 --> 00:28:59.460
where the Giarratana
family is hard at work.

00:28:59.460 --> 00:29:03.540
Cousin Grips grifting,
Grandma Gaffs gafting,

00:29:03.540 --> 00:29:05.600
and her parents, the
directors, leading it all.

00:29:05.600 --> 00:29:07.200
- No, no, no, no, no! (laughing)

00:29:07.200 --> 00:29:08.033
- Watch it!

00:29:08.033 --> 00:29:09.325
I'm walkin' here!

00:29:09.325 --> 00:29:10.158
(bell chiming)

00:29:10.158 --> 00:29:12.030
Hey, who left the hammer in the walkway?

00:29:12.030 --> 00:29:13.230
It's Mjolnir?

00:29:13.230 --> 00:29:14.628
It's a trip hazard!

00:29:14.628 --> 00:29:15.510
(everyone laughing)

00:29:15.510 --> 00:29:16.927
(Chanse clearing throat)

00:29:16.927 --> 00:29:20.681
♪ Workin' on a Marvel movie
ain't for the faint of heart ♪

00:29:20.681 --> 00:29:22.540
♪ You're workin' on a Marvel movie ♪

00:29:22.540 --> 00:29:24.336
♪ Ya gotta know your part ♪

00:29:24.336 --> 00:29:27.582
♪ Ya wake up at 4:30,
you eat breakfast at ♪

00:29:27.582 --> 00:29:31.572
♪ You wire up a Chris
Evans-Hemsworth-Pratt ♪

00:29:31.572 --> 00:29:33.330
Ugh!
(bell chiming)

00:29:33.330 --> 00:29:34.290
Enter Angela.

00:29:34.290 --> 00:29:35.850
Coming through, coming through!

00:29:35.850 --> 00:29:36.720
Whoa!

00:29:36.720 --> 00:29:38.580
Oh, it's okay, it's mine!

00:29:38.580 --> 00:29:39.413
Angela?

00:29:39.413 --> 00:29:40.246
Ha-ha!

00:29:40.246 --> 00:29:41.130
They're all mine, actually.

00:29:41.130 --> 00:29:42.733
I'm crazy! (laughing)

00:29:42.733 --> 00:29:44.093
(bell chiming)
(everyone laughing)

00:29:44.093 --> 00:29:45.960
The Giarratanas keep setting up set,

00:29:45.960 --> 00:29:48.219
while Angela goes into Odin's throne room.

00:29:48.219 --> 00:29:49.177
(strumming gently music)

00:29:49.177 --> 00:29:51.431
♪ I've worked on Marvel movies ♪

00:29:51.431 --> 00:29:54.643
♪ I've used my talents to serve the Lord ♪

00:29:54.643 --> 00:29:55.809
(crew laughing)

00:29:55.809 --> 00:29:58.372
♪ But I wanna make videos ♪

00:29:58.372 --> 00:30:01.650
♪ That people put on when they're bored ♪

00:30:01.650 --> 00:30:03.102
(Angela and crew laughing)

00:30:03.102 --> 00:30:06.370
♪ I wanna be on a channel ♪

00:30:06.370 --> 00:30:09.576
♪ That kinda makes people laugh ♪

00:30:09.576 --> 00:30:10.479
(crew laughing)

00:30:10.479 --> 00:30:14.570
♪ I wanna take a stupid little thought ♪

00:30:14.570 --> 00:30:18.153
♪ And cut that boring half ♪

00:30:20.114 --> 00:30:20.970
- [Crew Member] Whoo!

00:30:20.970 --> 00:30:21.803
- Cut!

00:30:21.803 --> 00:30:22.680
What the (beep) was that?

00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:24.480
We can't use any of that take!

00:30:24.480 --> 00:30:25.560
It was Angela!

00:30:25.560 --> 00:30:26.400
Angela?

00:30:26.400 --> 00:30:27.270
Angela!

00:30:27.270 --> 00:30:29.640
Sorry, I'm crazy!

00:30:29.640 --> 00:30:31.050
(everyone laughing)

00:30:31.050 --> 00:30:33.090
Well, you better get
control of your kid, Bill,

00:30:33.090 --> 00:30:35.970
before I send her into the Bifrost!

00:30:35.970 --> 00:30:38.940
Angela, you're 13 years old.

00:30:38.940 --> 00:30:41.280
You're basically a grown woman.

00:30:41.280 --> 00:30:43.950
You have a union job, dental, and crafty.

00:30:43.950 --> 00:30:45.870
You need to get your act together.

00:30:45.870 --> 00:30:48.220
Listen, we love you, but
you need to hear this.

00:30:49.244 --> 00:30:52.962
♪ You've got a good job and a call sheet ♪

00:30:52.962 --> 00:30:55.571
♪ Don't throw that away ♪

00:30:55.571 --> 00:30:59.273
♪ To make videos for blue hair teens ♪

00:30:59.273 --> 00:31:02.038
♪ That are all mostly gay ♪

00:31:02.038 --> 00:31:03.083
(everyone laughing)

00:31:03.083 --> 00:31:06.471
♪ You need to calm down ♪

00:31:06.471 --> 00:31:09.981
♪ You're an adult ♪

00:31:09.981 --> 00:31:13.292
♪ You need to calm down ♪
(Angela gasping)

00:31:13.292 --> 00:31:16.483
♪ You are an adult ♪

00:31:16.483 --> 00:31:17.670
(soft music ending)

00:31:17.670 --> 00:31:18.962
And that's the opening number.

00:31:18.962 --> 00:31:19.858
- Oh my god!

00:31:19.858 --> 00:31:23.039
(everyone cheering and applauding)

00:31:23.039 --> 00:31:24.361
Oh my god!

00:31:24.361 --> 00:31:25.903
- Is it good?

00:31:25.903 --> 00:31:27.876
(everyone applauding)

00:31:27.876 --> 00:31:28.876
- Oh my god!

00:31:30.639 --> 00:31:33.972
♪ Happy Birthday to you ♪

00:31:34.876 --> 00:31:35.709
- We don't have to sing the whole song.

00:31:35.709 --> 00:31:37.959
♪ Happy Birthday to you ♪
- That's so nice.

00:31:38.858 --> 00:31:39.900
That's really sweet.

00:31:39.900 --> 00:31:43.522
♪ Happy Birthday, dear Angela ♪

00:31:43.522 --> 00:31:44.355
- Ah!

00:31:45.723 --> 00:31:49.056
♪ Happy Birthday to you ♪

00:31:50.739 --> 00:31:51.700
- Aw!
- Yay!

00:31:51.700 --> 00:31:53.616
(everyone cheering and applauding)

00:31:53.616 --> 00:31:56.120
- He was here the whole time!

00:31:56.120 --> 00:31:57.512
- Aw, he's actually pretty cool.

00:31:57.512 --> 00:31:58.651
- Aw!

00:31:58.651 --> 00:31:59.793
He's pretty nice.

00:31:59.793 --> 00:32:00.660
He doesn't talk much.

00:32:00.660 --> 00:32:01.895
- He does smell like piss.

00:32:01.895 --> 00:32:02.728
- Yes!
(everyone giggling)

00:32:02.728 --> 00:32:06.810
- You guys, this is truly
way too much, way too kind.

00:32:06.810 --> 00:32:08.070
I love all of you so much.

00:32:08.070 --> 00:32:08.903
This is too much.

00:32:08.903 --> 00:32:10.830
We have to end the video
or I'll start crying.

00:32:10.830 --> 00:32:12.330
Wish your friends Happy Birthday.

00:32:12.330 --> 00:32:14.024
Buh-bye!

00:32:14.024 --> 00:32:15.858
(everyone cheering and applauding)

00:32:15.858 --> 00:32:17.286
- Where's my coffee?

00:32:17.286 --> 00:32:18.953
- Where's my coffee?

